<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratu Sir Lala Sukuna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888–1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratu Sir Lala Sukuna was a Fijian high chief, soldier and administrator, regarded as the leading Fijian statesman of the colonial period. Educated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>, he served with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-foreign-legion">French Foreign Legion</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. As secretary for Fijian affairs and the first Speaker of the Legislative Council, he shaped the Fijian administration and set up the Native Land Trust Board in 1940.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ratu-sir-lala-sukuna.jpg" alt="Ratu Sir Lala Sukuna" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Archives of Fiji · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ratu_Sir_Lala_Sukuna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
